From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:57:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 24/57] PROTOTYPE pvr: cache the SPM end-of-tile shader too

On the dynamic rendering path every vkCmdBeginRendering sets up a whole
render state, and with it compiles the SPM end-of-tile shader with pco:
one compile per render, ~1.1 ms of CPU each on GX6250/A53 (uprobes on
pvr_rogue_spm_init_eot_state). zink renders every offscreen pass this
way, so a Qt Quick window with five layered items paid ~6 compiles per
frame.

The shader is built from the same pvr_eot_props as the per-job
end-of-tile shader, so move that cache into pvr_arch_eot_shader_get()
and use it from both. The helper returns a private copy of the binary,
so a concurrent clear of the cache cannot free it under the caller.

Five scrolling layered labels, 4 interleaved rounds: qmlscene CPU
80 -> 45 %, a plain moving-text window 33 -> 26 %; GPU time and frame
rate unchanged.

Generated-by: LLM
